                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The Mexican Dream is a buggy tower defense game.\n\nTo start things off, the game is racist. Two towers are worth using, there's three different enemy types and only nine levels. Everything feels so boring, there's no leveling up, no progress shown, nothing. The spawns are random and sometimes you get overran and sometimes you get an easy run.\n\nThe AI is also buggy and doesn't always shoot, automatic towers shoot super slowly and sometimes you can't place any towers down... No way to pause and plan your towers either, you have to rush to build them before you get overrun, which is only saveable by shooting with a strategically placed tower manually.\n\nOverall, boring, unfun, short and overpriced. Not recommended.",
